WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.297
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.567 --> 00:02.833
Still, there really is someone I like.

3
00:02.953 --> 00:05.286
Is it... Takeuchi?

4
00:05.633 --> 00:08.300
Don't you have anyone you like, Suzuki?

5
00:09.333 --> 00:10.333
No.

6
00:14.300 --> 00:15.633
I see...

7
00:16.633 --> 00:21.567
I'm going to support Serizawa's love life.

8
00:26.033 --> 00:28.267
Suzuki, does this go here?

9
00:28.367 --> 00:29.500
Yeah.

10
00:29.967 --> 00:31.233
Ah, sorry, Suzuki.

11
00:31.333 --> 00:33.300
Looks like we're almost out of red paint.

12
00:33.400 --> 00:34.643
Got it. I'll go grab some later.

13
00:34.667 --> 00:38.000
Hey, Suzuki, look! Doesn't it look great?

14
00:38.100 --> 00:39.333
- Looks awesome! - Right?

15
00:39.433 --> 00:41.467
What do you think about adding some flowers here?

16
00:41.567 --> 00:43.133
- Around here works too. - True.

17
00:43.233 --> 00:44.409
There's still space over here.

18
00:44.433 --> 00:46.776
- Wouldn't that look great? - Ah, let's add them later, then.

19
00:46.800 --> 00:49.167
Suzuki looks super busy.

20
00:50.400 --> 00:55.000
He barely has any time for us lately.

21
00:56.167 --> 01:00.533
Still, I never thought Suzuki would volunteer for the festival committee.

22
01:02.600 --> 01:05.400
Oh, everyone's working hard!

23
01:06.667 --> 01:08.033
So cute!

24
01:08.667 --> 01:09.367
Look at this.

25
01:09.467 --> 01:10.300
Whoa, amazing!

26
01:10.400 --> 01:11.067
Look, look!

27
01:11.153 --> 01:12.953
I'm not talking about you.

28
01:13.067 --> 01:14.267
Did Takeuchi make this?

29
01:14.367 --> 01:15.033
Yes.

30
01:15.133 --> 01:16.667
He did such an incredible job.

31
01:17.300 --> 01:18.767
That's our Takeuchi.

32
01:19.367 --> 01:20.687
He's practically a master artist.

33
01:22.133 --> 01:23.400
Thank you, Teacher.

34
01:23.500 --> 01:25.767
Suzuki, where's the tape?

35
01:26.167 --> 01:27.300
Ah...

36
01:28.133 --> 01:29.200
Um...

37
01:32.433 --> 01:33.633
Suzuki!

38
01:33.733 --> 01:34.933
Here you go.

39
01:35.200 --> 01:37.400
Oh, thanks.

40
01:37.867 --> 01:38.967
Are you okay?

41
01:39.067 --> 01:41.433
Haven't you been pushing yourself too hard lately?

42
01:41.867 --> 01:44.633
You haven't had time to write your novel either.

43
01:45.567 --> 01:46.700
Well...

44
01:46.800 --> 01:49.333
Sorry, I've just been a bit busy.

45
01:49.733 --> 01:51.093
Is there anything I can help with?

46
01:51.133 --> 01:53.413
- If something's on your mind, you can always— - I'm fine.

47
01:53.567 --> 01:55.167
I'm really okay.

48
01:55.433 --> 01:58.467
Ah, go help Takeuchi instead.

49
01:59.000 --> 02:00.267
Go on.

50
02:04.767 --> 02:05.900
Suzuki!

51
02:06.000 --> 02:07.133
Ah...

52
02:10.167 --> 02:11.767
What's going on with you and Suzuki?

53
02:14.833 --> 02:16.067
Huh?

54
02:16.167 --> 02:18.067
Suzuki said he doesn't have anyone he likes?

55
02:18.167 --> 02:19.633
Yeah, basically...

56
02:20.567 --> 02:22.400
So in other words...

57
02:23.300 --> 02:24.033
You got rejected.

58
02:24.133 --> 02:25.633
I didn't get rejected!

59
02:26.133 --> 02:28.933
I was a little bummed when I heard it, sure.

60
02:30.267 --> 02:33.733
But thinking about it, there's no reason to be down.

61
02:33.833 --> 02:34.633
Yeah?

62
02:34.733 --> 02:37.767
Even if he doesn't like me right now...

63
02:37.867 --> 02:39.967
he might fall for me later on, right?

64
02:40.067 --> 02:40.900
Right?

65
02:41.000 --> 02:47.233
Besides, having no crush means I have no rivals.

66
02:47.333 --> 02:49.467
Isn't that super promising?

67
02:51.100 --> 02:52.867
Classic Serizawa.

68
02:52.967 --> 02:55.133
The ultimate optimist, as always.

69
02:56.033 --> 02:58.933
- Terrifying. - A total monster.

70
02:59.367 --> 03:03.333
Still, the issue is with Suzuki...

71
03:07.100 --> 03:08.967
Don't you have one, Suzuki?

72
03:10.333 --> 03:11.600
Someone you like?

73
03:13.433 --> 03:14.667
No.

74
03:17.033 --> 03:18.300
I see...

75
03:20.200 --> 03:24.700
Ever since that day, I haven't been able to write a single word.

76
03:24.800 --> 03:25.800
No, this won't do.

77
03:25.900 --> 03:29.300
I can't go on like this. I already decided to support him.

78
03:30.067 --> 03:33.367
For now, I just need to focus on festival prep.

79
03:36.367 --> 03:40.400
I just can't let go of my feelings for Serizawa.

80
04:26.467 --> 04:29.333
Popular Serizawa Acts Weird Around Me.

81
04:29.800 --> 04:31.200
(Traditional Festival Stall)

82
04:31.300 --> 04:33.533
(Episode 9) All right!

83
04:33.633 --> 04:35.600
The day is finally here.

84
04:35.700 --> 04:36.933
Yeah.

85
04:37.433 --> 04:39.667
Whoa, not bad!

86
04:40.567 --> 04:42.167
Looks great.

87
04:43.567 --> 04:46.433
Still, Suzuki, you really worked hard.

88
04:46.533 --> 04:48.213
The prep must have been exhausting, right?

89
04:48.600 --> 04:49.700
Yes.

90
04:50.000 --> 04:52.333
Though... I'd rather stay busy.

91
04:52.800 --> 04:53.967
What was that?

92
04:54.933 --> 04:55.933
Oh, it's nothing...

93
04:56.033 --> 04:58.400
It was all thanks to everyone's help.

94
05:29.733 --> 05:30.933
Suzuki.

95
05:32.600 --> 05:33.600
Well?

96
05:33.667 --> 05:34.933
How do I look?

97
05:36.400 --> 05:37.500
Yeah.

98
05:38.100 --> 05:39.567
It suits you so well.

99
05:42.500 --> 05:43.900
Did your heart skip a beat?

100
05:44.300 --> 05:47.267
- N-No, it didn't. - Come on, you're supposed to say yes!

101
05:47.800 --> 05:49.600
All right, lead the way, Captain!

102
05:49.700 --> 05:50.500
Huh?

103
05:50.600 --> 05:52.233
Okay! Everyone, bring it in!

104
05:52.333 --> 05:53.367
Yeah!

105
05:53.467 --> 05:55.067
That's the spirit!

106
05:58.367 --> 06:02.367
Let's hear a few words from Suzuki!

107
06:05.033 --> 06:08.800
Um... thank you so much, everyone.

108
06:08.900 --> 06:13.367
You helped me out so much during prep.

109
06:14.067 --> 06:17.300
Let's do our best today, too!

110
06:18.200 --> 06:21.533
All right! Let's get fired up!

111
06:22.100 --> 06:23.500
One, two, three, fight!

112
06:28.467 --> 06:29.733
Welcome!

113
06:31.233 --> 06:32.600
Here you go.

114
06:39.700 --> 06:40.500
Nice, nice!

115
06:40.600 --> 06:41.933
(Soothing Turtle Stand)

116
06:44.067 --> 06:46.747
- This little turtle is cute just like you. - It really is adorable.

117
06:51.833 --> 06:54.433
(Free Weightlifting)

118
06:54.967 --> 06:56.267
Welcome!

119
06:56.367 --> 06:57.800
Want to try yo-yo balloon fishing?

120
06:58.900 --> 07:01.767
Excuse me, do you know where Kou-chan is?

121
07:01.867 --> 07:02.533
Kou-chan?

122
07:02.633 --> 07:04.233
I heard he was here.

123
07:04.333 --> 07:06.043
- Do you know where Kou-chan is? - Kou-chan?

124
07:06.067 --> 07:08.833
He has pale skin and black hair.

125
07:09.100 --> 07:10.367
Black hair, huh...

126
07:10.467 --> 07:11.543
Do you know where Kou-chan is?

127
07:11.567 --> 07:12.367
Wait, Kou-chan?

128
07:12.467 --> 07:13.567
Yeah.

129
07:14.167 --> 07:15.300
Kou-chan!

130
07:15.400 --> 07:16.600
Huh?

131
07:16.800 --> 07:18.067
It's Kou-chan!

132
07:18.833 --> 07:19.733
No, I'm not.

133
07:19.833 --> 07:20.833
- Huh? - What?

134
07:20.900 --> 07:21.900
- Huh? - What?

135
07:22.033 --> 07:23.200
Aren't you Kou-chan?

136
07:23.733 --> 07:25.067
N-No, I'm not.

137
07:25.167 --> 07:26.467
Then what's your name?

138
07:28.867 --> 07:30.467
Suzuki Hajime.

139
07:30.567 --> 07:31.847
- Suzuki Hajime? - Suzuki Hajime.

140
07:31.933 --> 07:33.367
- Yeah, I'm Suzuki. - What?!

141
07:33.667 --> 07:35.767
You look just like Kou-chan!

142
07:36.900 --> 07:38.967
Huh? You're really not him?

143
07:39.067 --> 07:40.933
- His name's Hajime-chan. - Hajime-chan?

144
07:41.267 --> 07:43.433
Oh, so you're Hajime-chan!

145
07:43.533 --> 07:45.633
Where on earth did Kou-chan go?

146
07:45.733 --> 07:48.400
- This toy is actually pretty fun. - Better than I expected!

147
07:48.500 --> 07:48.933
Huh?

148
07:49.033 --> 07:50.867
It's so lively over here!

149
07:50.967 --> 07:52.533
Wait...

150
07:52.633 --> 07:53.667
Isn't that Suzuki?

151
07:53.767 --> 07:54.967
Incredible!

152
07:59.400 --> 08:01.133
We completely sold out!

153
08:01.333 --> 08:04.233
All right! That wraps it up for us too.

154
08:05.967 --> 08:07.300
- Sold out! - Sweet!

155
08:07.400 --> 08:09.367
That's awesome! Way to go!

156
08:09.467 --> 08:11.833
(Sold Out. Thank you for your support!)

157
08:13.267 --> 08:14.633
Everyone...

158
08:15.100 --> 08:17.600
Thank you for all your hard work.

159
08:18.400 --> 08:19.676
Everything's taken care of here.

160
08:19.700 --> 08:20.940
You're all free to look around.

161
08:21.000 --> 08:22.933
- Seriously? - Awesome!

162
08:23.100 --> 08:24.609
- Koharu, let's go check it out. - Sure thing!

163
08:24.633 --> 08:26.633
- Takeuchi, let's grab some food. - Sounds good.

164
08:31.000 --> 08:34.100
Serizawa, why don't you go with Takeuchi?

165
08:34.500 --> 08:36.433
Nah, I'm good.

166
08:36.900 --> 08:40.100
But it's the festival...

167
08:40.200 --> 08:40.933
Why?

168
08:41.033 --> 08:42.667
Didn't you say we have free time?

169
08:44.100 --> 08:48.800
Then I want to hang out with you, Suzuki.

170
08:51.600 --> 08:53.367
Don't say things like that...

171
08:54.433 --> 08:55.700
Huh?

172
08:55.800 --> 08:57.333
Ah, sorry.

173
08:57.433 --> 09:00.300
Oh, I still have rounds to do as a committee member.

174
09:00.400 --> 09:01.433
I have to get going.

175
09:01.533 --> 09:04.500
So I can't stay with you, Serizawa.

176
09:04.600 --> 09:05.900
Sorry.

177
09:11.600 --> 09:12.933
Hey...

178
09:17.967 --> 09:20.800
I really do want to be with Serizawa.

179
09:21.467 --> 09:23.433
But if we stay together like this...

180
09:23.933 --> 09:26.400
I'll never be able to move on from these feelings.

181
09:26.667 --> 09:28.733
That Suzuki guy is seriously obnoxious.

182
09:28.833 --> 09:30.667
He used to be a total loner.

183
09:30.767 --> 09:32.487
Now he suddenly acts like he's Mr. Popular.

184
09:32.533 --> 09:34.509
He even joined the committee. Who does he think he is?

185
09:34.533 --> 09:37.767
Come to think of it, Serizawa's pretty ridiculous too.

186
09:37.867 --> 09:41.367
Whenever it involves Suzuki, he gets all fired up.

187
09:41.467 --> 09:43.600
He even claimed he likes BL now.

188
09:43.700 --> 09:44.800
Right?

189
09:44.900 --> 09:46.167
What's Serizawa's deal anyway?

190
09:46.267 --> 09:49.700
Don't tell me he actually has a crush on Suzuki?

191
09:50.367 --> 09:52.667
- Gross. - No way, that's disgusting.

192
09:52.767 --> 09:54.100
You're wrong.

193
09:54.367 --> 09:55.167
Suzuki?

194
09:55.267 --> 09:58.633
Serizawa does not like me.

195
10:01.667 --> 10:02.900
Huh?

196
10:03.567 --> 10:09.033
And there's nothing weird or gross about him!

197
10:09.133 --> 10:13.867
He's the coolest and kindest person in the world.

198
10:13.967 --> 10:15.700
He brings sunshine to everyone.

199
10:16.233 --> 10:20.367
- And besides... - What are you even babbling about?

200
10:20.467 --> 10:24.100
We were just messing around.

201
10:24.200 --> 10:25.600
Right?

202
10:25.700 --> 10:26.700
Yeah.

203
10:26.800 --> 10:29.367
Like Serizawa would ever like Suzuki.

204
10:30.000 --> 10:31.433
That's completely impossible.

205
10:32.133 --> 10:33.533
Are you guys done yet?

206
10:34.400 --> 10:35.667
Matsuno?

207
10:40.100 --> 10:41.433
Cut it out.

208
10:42.833 --> 10:45.467
You're just jealous of Suzuki.

209
10:45.800 --> 10:46.600
What?

210
10:46.700 --> 10:48.533
- What are you talking about? - Just admit it.

211
10:50.400 --> 10:51.800
You're envious, aren't you?

212
10:53.100 --> 10:55.767
Envious that Suzuki gets to be friends with the popular kids.

213
10:56.667 --> 10:57.733
Hey, wait a second.

214
10:57.833 --> 10:59.967
Why are you sticking up for Suzuki?

215
11:02.167 --> 11:04.400
Because...

216
11:08.633 --> 11:10.267
I just...

217
11:12.000 --> 11:14.400
I want to keep being friends with Suzuki.

218
11:28.000 --> 11:30.800
About earlier... thank you.

219
11:36.500 --> 11:38.100
And also...

220
11:40.467 --> 11:41.767
I'm sorry.

221
11:45.067 --> 11:49.633
About what happened back in freshman year.

222
11:52.800 --> 11:55.233
I've always wanted to apologize to you.

223
11:56.200 --> 11:59.433
Back then, I was only thinking about myself.

224
11:59.533 --> 12:00.567
No way.

225
12:00.667 --> 12:01.767
Gross.

226
12:04.533 --> 12:05.900
Disgusting.

227
12:07.567 --> 12:09.267
Saying awful things like that...

228
12:11.167 --> 12:12.967
and hurting you like that, Suzuki.

229
12:17.433 --> 12:18.967
I'm truly sorry.

230
12:26.133 --> 12:29.667
(Romeo and Romeo) (Class 2-2 Theater / Drama Club)

231
12:30.367 --> 12:32.100
Romeo is so handsome.

232
12:32.200 --> 12:33.300
He's all right.

233
12:33.400 --> 12:34.667
Oh, Serizawa.

234
12:35.100 --> 12:35.800
Huh?

235
12:35.900 --> 12:37.100
Aren't you with Suzuki?

236
12:37.200 --> 12:38.300
Ah, yeah.

237
12:38.400 --> 12:39.867
He seemed pretty busy.

238
12:42.367 --> 12:44.267
Dude, you bought way too much stuff.

239
12:44.367 --> 12:45.233
What did you get?

240
12:45.333 --> 12:47.053
This is ridiculous. How much did you spend?

241
12:47.100 --> 12:48.167
What's going on?

242
12:48.667 --> 12:49.433
Look at all this.

243
12:49.533 --> 12:50.700
Ooh, the good stuff!

244
12:51.933 --> 12:53.233
Hands off!

245
12:53.333 --> 12:55.533
Hey, did you guys hear?

246
12:55.633 --> 12:57.376
Teacher Usami's girlfriend is at the gym right now!

247
12:57.400 --> 12:58.967
Apparently an event is starting soon.

248
12:59.067 --> 13:00.667
- Really? - Let's all go check it out!

249
13:01.433 --> 13:03.333
- Let's go. - Come on!

250
13:05.033 --> 13:10.633
To be honest, I've always admired you, Suzuki.

251
13:11.267 --> 13:11.900
Huh...?

252
13:12.000 --> 13:18.233
The truth is, I have an idol I really like too.

253
13:19.533 --> 13:20.733
An idol?

254
13:27.367 --> 13:29.400
(Oky) This guy right here.

255
13:30.067 --> 13:31.933
I never told my friends.

256
13:33.833 --> 13:36.533
Because I was afraid if I did...

257
13:37.033 --> 13:39.767
they'd reject me or laugh at me.

258
13:42.400 --> 13:46.067
Seeing you stay true to what you love...

259
13:46.167 --> 13:49.967
even when you were all on your own...

260
13:50.067 --> 13:52.000
I thought that was truly incredible.

261
13:54.667 --> 14:00.867
Not really. I'm not that confident either.

262
14:01.900 --> 14:05.000
Besides, there's nothing wrong with keeping it to yourself.

263
14:06.633 --> 14:13.200
Share it if you want, keep it private if you don't.

264
14:13.767 --> 14:17.800
No matter how you choose to support your idol, Matsuno...

265
14:18.667 --> 14:24.133
those feelings belong entirely to you.

266
14:30.100 --> 14:33.500
You really are amazing, Suzuki.

267
14:35.833 --> 14:39.467
And Serizawa too.

268
14:39.567 --> 14:40.767
Huh?

269
14:44.400 --> 14:45.833
Um...

270
14:53.267 --> 14:57.633
This is Suzuki's. Could you give it back to him for me?

271
14:57.733 --> 14:59.067
I refuse.

272
14:59.600 --> 15:00.867
Huh?

273
15:00.967 --> 15:03.000
No way. I really won't.

274
15:03.100 --> 15:04.500
Absolutely not.

275
15:04.600 --> 15:06.200
I totally refuse.

276
15:06.933 --> 15:10.139
Why do you have to be so against it?

277
15:10.233 --> 15:14.500
Because if I'm the one who returns it...

278
15:14.600 --> 15:17.867
he'll think it means you're cutting ties with him.

279
15:18.733 --> 15:22.567
"Does Matsuno not want to talk to me anymore?"

280
15:22.667 --> 15:26.267
"Are we never going to be friends again?"

281
15:26.900 --> 15:30.900
If Suzuki thinks that, he'll get hurt.

282
15:32.367 --> 15:33.967
I don't want that.

283
15:35.300 --> 15:38.600
I never want Suzuki to get hurt.

284
15:38.700 --> 15:40.800
Not even for a single second.

285
15:47.633 --> 15:50.133
I genuinely think he's remarkable.

286
15:51.733 --> 15:54.500
Serizawa is such a great guy.

287
15:55.567 --> 15:58.700
I had no idea Serizawa did that for me...

288
16:00.233 --> 16:04.433
Thanks for hearing me out.

289
16:06.000 --> 16:08.967
From now on, I'll keep supporting my idol...

290
16:09.067 --> 16:10.767
just the way I want to.

291
16:11.033 --> 16:13.333
Yeah, I think that's great.

292
16:19.700 --> 16:26.300
So make sure you cherish what you love too, Suzuki.

293
16:27.300 --> 16:29.400
The things that matter to you.

294
16:44.733 --> 16:47.700
The things I love...

295
16:50.267 --> 16:51.533
Suzuki!

296
16:56.500 --> 16:59.033
All done packing up?

297
17:00.933 --> 17:02.800
Ah... yeah.

298
17:02.900 --> 17:05.167
All right, come with me for a second.

299
17:05.267 --> 17:06.400
Huh?

300
17:09.100 --> 17:09.800
Here we go.

301
17:09.900 --> 17:11.200
Ready, set...

302
17:11.300 --> 17:12.100
Ah!

303
17:12.200 --> 17:15.500
Suzuki! Great job today...

304
17:17.467 --> 17:18.467
Whoa, we startled him!

305
17:18.533 --> 17:20.800
You were so busy on the committee...

306
17:20.900 --> 17:23.233
did you even have time to visit other classes?

307
17:23.333 --> 17:28.267
Serizawa said we should throw an appreciation party for you.

308
17:28.367 --> 17:33.100
Apparently he bought snacks from the whole school by himself.

309
17:35.733 --> 17:37.867
Well? Did your heart skip a beat?

310
17:41.967 --> 17:43.433
It did.

311
17:49.600 --> 17:55.300
Didn't expect it to double as Takeuchi's heartbreak party too.

312
17:55.400 --> 17:55.967
Heartbreak?

313
17:56.067 --> 17:58.133
- Way to read the room! - It's fine.

314
17:58.233 --> 17:59.667
It's all right.

315
17:59.767 --> 18:01.567
I knew it from the start anyway.

316
18:01.833 --> 18:05.500
After all, I fell for a teacher who could never love me back.

317
18:05.600 --> 18:07.133
A... a teacher?

318
18:07.233 --> 18:10.333
Oh, didn't I tell you, Suzuki?

319
18:10.933 --> 18:18.133
I had a crush on Teacher Usami.

320
18:18.767 --> 18:20.400
Teacher Usami?

321
18:21.367 --> 18:22.667
Yeah.

322
18:23.200 --> 18:28.400
Except today, on stage in the gym...

323
18:29.133 --> 18:31.433
Teacher Usami proposed publicly.

324
18:33.500 --> 18:35.600
Congratulations!

325
18:35.900 --> 18:37.633
Go get her, Teacher!

326
18:37.733 --> 18:39.767
(High Schoolers' Honest Thoughts)

327
18:40.967 --> 18:42.533
Go for it, Teacher!

328
18:43.533 --> 18:46.200
- So romantic! - You got this!

329
18:46.900 --> 18:48.333
I love you.

330
18:49.700 --> 18:53.500
More than anyone else in the world.

331
18:59.167 --> 19:00.767
Oh my gosh, oh my gosh!

332
19:01.567 --> 19:03.833
For the rest of our lives...

333
19:03.933 --> 19:06.333
will you marry me and be my partner forever?

334
19:09.767 --> 19:11.133
Yes.

335
19:14.733 --> 19:16.467
Congratulations to you both!

336
19:17.267 --> 19:18.633
Congratulations, Teacher!

337
19:29.567 --> 19:31.467
It hurts so much...

338
19:32.333 --> 19:34.400
There, there, Takeuchi.

339
19:35.300 --> 19:36.933
Want some takoyaki?

340
19:38.467 --> 19:43.633
Or do you want a hug from me?

341
19:43.733 --> 19:44.967
No.

342
19:45.867 --> 19:47.500
Don't be nice to me right now.

343
19:48.933 --> 19:50.667
I might end up falling for you.

344
19:54.600 --> 19:56.333
I wouldn't mind if you did.

345
19:59.067 --> 20:00.067
Huh?

346
20:05.800 --> 20:08.800
Without your glasses, you're actually pretty cute.

347
20:11.167 --> 20:12.300
What?

348
20:18.133 --> 20:20.000
Hey, let me see again!

349
20:20.100 --> 20:20.967
See?

350
20:21.067 --> 20:23.133
Wait, is another BL romance starting here?

351
20:24.100 --> 20:25.933
Takeuchi...

352
20:27.700 --> 20:30.167
Wait, so everyone knew about this?

353
20:30.267 --> 20:31.567
Serizawa knew too?

354
20:31.667 --> 20:34.033
- Yeah. - What?

355
20:34.633 --> 20:35.967
Huh?

356
20:36.267 --> 20:37.767
Then...

357
20:39.067 --> 20:41.233
What is Serizawa going to do?

358
20:41.867 --> 20:42.867
Me?

359
20:43.333 --> 20:44.600
What do you mean?

360
20:44.700 --> 20:46.067
Wait...

361
20:46.667 --> 20:48.000
What is going on?

362
20:48.100 --> 20:51.400
Takeuchi wasn't the one Serizawa liked?

363
20:52.600 --> 20:54.267
Then who on earth is it?

364
20:57.167 --> 20:58.900
Forget about that for now. Just eat!

365
20:59.000 --> 21:01.600
We got all this special food for Suzuki.

366
21:03.500 --> 21:04.900
Which one do you want?

367
21:06.933 --> 21:08.700
Whatever...

368
21:09.133 --> 21:10.333
I'll stop overthinking.

369
21:20.500 --> 21:27.000
By the way, did you talk with Matsuno today?

370
21:27.967 --> 21:29.033
Yeah.

371
21:29.133 --> 21:30.400
Thanks to you, Serizawa.

372
21:30.700 --> 21:32.167
We talked.

373
21:33.967 --> 21:37.067
Does that mean he'll become...

374
21:37.500 --> 21:39.400
your best friend again?

375
21:40.533 --> 21:41.833
Huh?

376
21:43.367 --> 21:45.300
Didn't you say before?

377
21:46.100 --> 21:47.900
That you two used to be closest.

378
21:49.933 --> 21:51.633
Oh...

379
21:52.900 --> 21:56.933
Still, he won't be number one.

380
21:59.133 --> 22:01.067
Because I have...

381
22:03.233 --> 22:04.833
I have Serizawa.

382
22:06.600 --> 22:10.567
Even if... no matter who Serizawa likes...

383
22:14.133 --> 22:16.733
Wait, that hurts, Serizawa!

384
22:17.200 --> 22:20.033
I was just so happy...

385
22:20.133 --> 22:23.833
to hear you say that!

386
22:25.200 --> 22:29.467
And I've always wanted to hug you like this, Suzuki.

387
22:32.033 --> 22:33.967
Me too...

388
22:34.400 --> 22:38.133
I like Serizawa.

389
22:38.233 --> 22:39.467
Hm?

390
22:40.367 --> 22:41.867
What did you just say?

391
22:42.333 --> 22:43.933
It's a secret.

392
22:44.033 --> 22:48.033
Because these feelings are my own treasure.

393
22:48.133 --> 22:50.167
Aw, come on!

394
22:50.267 --> 22:51.433
Tell me!

395
22:51.533 --> 22:52.667
No way.

396
22:52.767 --> 22:55.067
- Stop teasing me! - Whoa, close one!

397
22:55.167 --> 22:56.533
How about some of this?

398
22:56.633 --> 22:57.633
What if I eat this?

399
22:57.667 --> 22:58.943
If I eat this, I don't have to tell you, right?

400
22:58.967 --> 22:59.733
Deal.

401
22:59.833 --> 23:01.393
(Next Episode Preview) (BL Novel Finale)

402
23:01.967 --> 23:03.533
I finished writing it.

403
23:03.633 --> 23:04.300
- I want to read it! - Me too!

404
23:04.400 --> 23:05.400
Sorry.

405
23:05.467 --> 23:07.133
I'll let everyone read it later.

406
23:07.233 --> 23:09.467
I kind of feel like crying right now.

407
23:09.567 --> 23:10.667
Ah, sorry.

408
23:12.433 --> 23:14.700
(This program is entirely fictional.)
